Note: cipher 'AES-256-CBC' in --data-ciphers is not supported by ovpn-dco, disabling data channel offload.

ovpn-dco (the new Windows 11 OpenVPN Data Channel Offload driver) does not support AES-256-CBC.

That means if your client config uses AES-256-CBC, the data channel offload will be disabled — it can still work, but sometimes this causes TLS handshake issues.

The recommended cipher is AES-256-GCM or any AEAD cipher (AES-256-GCM, CHACHA20-POLY1305).

